  "details": "My safety settings are set very strictly and I often come across situations where the avatar is not looking correct so then I show their avatar and then I'm met with a bunch of effects that I did not want to see. \nAdding the ability to change avatar safety settings on a per-user basis would fix this issue and give users a whole new level of customization.\nI saw a post on the canny about this idea already, but I wanted to expand on this idea with a concept. (image linked below)\nWhen selecting a user with the Quick Menu, double-clicking the \"Use Safety Settings\" icon under Avatar Display would expand the UI element showing the settings to change that user's avatar safety settings. The options include audio, lights and particles, shaders, and custom animations toggles (hovering over the toggles would show you what each toggle does with the tooltips that appear under the tabs). After selecting which settings you want either double-clicking on the \"Use Safety Settings\" icon again or close the Quick Menu to apply.",
